; Similar to the Python package numpy's linspace function/method.
; linspace is documented at:
; https://numpy.org/doc/stable/reference/generated/numpy.linspace.html
;
; numpy.linspace's axis is omitted because
;  the documentation didn't make enough sense to implement a WebLogo equivalent.
; 
; numpy.linspace's dtype is unnecessarily explicit 
; in WebLogo so it was omitted.
;
; numpy.linspace's device is also omitted because WebLogo code 
; doesn't care if its lists were created in GPU or CPU.
to pyNumPyLinspace :start :stop :num :endpoint? :retstep?
	assert and integer? :num :num >= 0
	assert boolean? :endpoint?
	assert boolean? :retstep?
	localmake "samples []
	if (and :num > 0 number? :start number? :stop) [
		if :endpoint? [
			; If True, stop is the last sample. 
			; Otherwise, it is not included. Default is True.
			localmake "stop :stop - (:stop - :start) / (:num + 1)
		]
		localmake "step (:stop - :start) / :num
		localmake "samples rseq :start :stop :step
	]

	ifelse :retstep? [
		output [:samples :step]
	] [
		output :samples
	]
end